              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 65,
                "start": 65
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Roman Martinez, the Solicitor General misquoted the statute as covering \u201cpersonnel actions based on age,\u201d whereas the correct text says \u201cshall be made free from any discrimination based on age.\u201d"
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Roman Martinez",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "88b8970ca43c81ac8d497c96b48d8b18d30a37738b8b497b545f778d95f26b6f",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-88b8970ca43c-0003-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 66,
                "start": 66
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Roman Martinez, congress deliberately chose the \u201cfree from any discrimination\u201d language after rejecting an earlier draft of the statute."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Roman Martinez",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "88b8970ca43c81ac8d497c96b48d8b18d30a37738b8b497b545f778d95f26b6f",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-88b8970ca43c-0003-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 68,
                "start": 68
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Roman Martinez, the injury at stake is a process\u2011based equal\u2011protection claim, similar to cases from Bakke through Parents Involved."
        }
      ],
